# The master captures are NOT committed, and the reason is a hard limit rather
# than a preference: the largest is 114 MB and GitHub rejects any file over
# 100 MB. Even under the limit, 236 MB of phone video in a research repository
# would dominate every clone of it forever.
#
# What is committed instead:
#   web/            derivatives - full-length mono audio, stills, posters
#   media-data.json every number extracted from the masters
#   *.txt           the stopwatch export, which is the raw data
#
# Every master is identified in media-data.json by SHA-256, so anyone holding
# a copy can prove it is the same file. AUDIO IS COMMITTED IN FULL - timing is
# the only acoustic quantity this work claims, and timing is in the audio.
# Video is where the bytes are and video is what is dropped.

*.mp4
*.mov

# Camera originals. The 1600 px derivatives in web/ are what the page uses.
# The leading slash matters: without it these patterns match at ANY depth and
# silently exclude the derivatives in web/ as well, which produces a page full
# of broken images and a build that reports success.
/20260803_*.jpg
/grassy-knoll-*.jpg
/clock-screenshot_*.jpg

_*.py
_*.js
_*.html
_*.png
__pycache__/
